[center][color=#ffff00][size=6][b]Radioport Fixes - Dropouts and Misc Fixes[/b][/size][/color]
[i]Fixes for vanilla Radioport bugs, from dropouts and muffled sound to radios cutting out at low master volume.[/i][/center]
[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]Description[/b][/size][/color]
Fixes for bugs in the Radioport that happen in an unmodded game.

[color=#ffff00][size=4][b]Dropouts[/b][/size][/color]
Walking around with the Radioport on, your station sometimes cuts out for ten to thirty seconds, then comes back on its own.

The game plays at most four radio stations at once, the four whose nearest radio is closest to you. It measures each station from one radio only, and it will not use your Radioport for that whenever any other radio in the world is tuned to the same station, a passing car or a radio in a bar or apartment, even one that is switched off. When that radio is further away than four other stations' radios, your station is no longer one of the four, and the Radioport goes silent until that radio is out of range. A world radio playing your station goes silent with it.

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/33838/33838-1789264474-1461224021.png[/img][/center]

This mod changes one instruction in the game so the Radioport counts like any other radio. It is on you, so your station is measured from where you stand, and the station you are listening to keeps its place.

[color=#ffff00][size=4][b]Muffled after a drive[/b][/size][/color]
After you drive a car and get out, the Radioport plays quieter and muffled, like a small speaker, until you load a save.

When a save loads, the game sets the Radioport to play clean. Getting out of the car leaves it on a quieter, filtered setting instead. This mod puts it back to the clean setting each time you get out of a vehicle, from any seat.

[color=#ffff00][size=4][b]Song name on foot[/b][/size][/color]
With the station selection UI open on foot, the song name stays on the old song when the track changes, until you switch station and back.

In a car the game updates the name as each song starts. It does not do this for the Radioport. While the station selection UI is open on foot, this mod checks the song twice a second and updates the name when it changes. In a car it does nothing.

[color=#ffff00][size=4][b]Station applied twice[/b][/size][/color]
Picking a station in the station selection UI applied it twice, once on the button press and again on the release. This mod applies it once, with keyboard, mouse or controller.

[color=#ffff00][size=4][b]Silent at low master volume[/b][/size][/color]
At a very low master volume, the Radioport and the car radio cut out completely when turned down a notch, or when the police scanner or gunfire is heard, instead of getting quieter.

The game drops any radio sound that falls below a set level, and at low master volume the radio sits right at that line. This mod lowers the line so the radio keeps playing and just gets quieter. Game 2.31 does not have this bug, so on 2.31 this fix does nothing.
[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]Optional: Radioport Off[/b][/size][/color]
A separate optional file for players who never use the Radioport. It keeps the Radioport off for good: its button does nothing, holding it does not open the station list, and getting out of a car does not turn it on. It does not need the main file, only Redscript. To turn the Radioport back on, uninstall it.
[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*]Game version 2.5 or 2.31[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380]RED4ext[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/1511]Redscript[/url][/*]
[/list]
[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size][/color]
Install with your mod manager, or extract the archive into your Cyberpunk 2077 folder so you end up with:
[code]Cyberpunk 2077\red4ext\plugins\RadioportDropoutFix\RadioportDropoutFix.dll
Cyberpunk 2077\r6\scripts\RadioportDropoutFix\RadioportSingleActivate.reds
Cyberpunk 2077\r6\scripts\RadioportDropoutFix\RadioportTier.reds
Cyberpunk 2077\r6\scripts\RadioportDropoutFix\RadioportTrackName.reds[/code]

The optional Radioport Off file installs [font=Courier New]Cyberpunk 2077\r6\scripts\RadioportOff\RadioportOff.reds[/font].

To confirm the dropout fix is working, open [font=Courier New]red4ext\logs\[/font] after launching the game. The newest [font=Courier New]radioportdropoutfix[/font] log should contain lines starting with [font=Courier New]patched:[/font].

[color=#ffff00][size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size][/color]
Delete both folders.

[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*]Only a mod that changes the same instruction in the game overlaps with it. If one is installed, this mod sees the change already made, leaves it alone and says so in its log.[/*]
[*]The muffled-sound fix adds to the game's own script for getting out of a vehicle without replacing it, so other mods that add to the same script work alongside it.[/*]
[*]The song name fix adds to the game's station selection UI without replacing any of it. It also follows RadioXL's skip-track keys.[/*]
[*]The station fix adds to the game's handling of the station selection UI without replacing it.[/*]
[/list]
[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]Source[/b][/size][/color]
The source is on [url=https://github.com/spuddeh/cp2077-radioport-dropout-fix]GitHub[/url].

